1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,241
Mummy placed her wedding bangles on the jeweller's counter.

2
00:00:05,241 --> 00:00:10,005
She thought, gold must have become so expensive over all these years.

3
00:00:10,005 --> 00:00:15,246
I'll get good money today. The jeweller weighed the bangles, ran the calculator,

4
00:00:15,246 --> 00:00:20,010
and said the amount with a smile. Mummy's face fell.

5
00:00:20,010 --> 00:00:24,457
The amount wasn't small, but it was far less than she had hoped.

6
00:00:24,457 --> 00:00:28,903
The jeweller said, madam, you don't get money back for the design.

7
00:00:28,903 --> 00:00:33,350
I only weigh the gold, and that too after checking its purity.

8
00:00:33,350 --> 00:00:34,239
Mummy said,

9
00:00:34,239 --> 00:00:38,686
when we bought it, we paid full price for the design too.

10
00:00:38,686 --> 00:00:40,020
The jeweller stayed silent.

11
00:00:40,020 --> 00:00:43,920
At home, Mummy told Papa everything. Papa said,

12
00:00:43,920 --> 00:00:47,430
gold never cheats you, it's safe.

13
00:00:47,430 --> 00:00:50,940
My sister looked up from her phone and asked, Papa,

14
00:00:50,940 --> 00:00:54,060
are safe and earning the same thing?

15
00:00:54,060 --> 00:00:56,790
A silence fell over the room for a while.

16
00:00:56,790 --> 00:01:00,094
This story belongs to almost every Indian home.

17
00:01:00,094 --> 00:01:04,223
We consider gold to be security, and rightly so,

18
00:01:04,223 --> 00:01:06,701
it helps in hard times.

19
00:01:06,701 --> 00:01:12,069
But the real question is which gold actually earns.

20
00:01:12,069 --> 00:01:14,960
Jewellery, gold ETF, or sovereign gold bond?

21
00:01:14,960 --> 00:01:18,269
Today's questions are simple. First,

22
00:01:18,269 --> 00:01:23,232
where does the making charge on jewellery go? Second,

23
00:01:23,232 --> 00:01:27,092
who counts the cost of the locker? Third,

24
00:01:27,092 --> 00:01:32,055
how do you get an extra 2.5 percent on a gold bond?

25
00:01:32,055 --> 00:01:37,570
And finally, when is jewellery a purchase, and when is it an investment.

26
00:01:37,570 --> 00:01:42,464
Let's go back to the day the bangles were bought.

27
00:01:42,464 --> 00:01:46,023
Wedding preparations were on, the house was full of cheer.

28
00:01:46,023 --> 00:01:50,027
Papa and Mummy were sitting at the jeweller's shop.

29
00:01:50,027 --> 00:01:53,586
In front of them, trays of shining bangles, necklaces and earrings.

30
00:01:53,586 --> 00:01:56,700
Every item had a price tag.

31
00:01:56,700 --> 00:02:01,779
When the jeweller made the bill, it had several lines. First,

32
00:02:01,779 --> 00:02:07,367
the weight of the gold and that day's rate. Second, the making charge.

33
00:02:07,367 --> 00:02:12,954
Then GST on top. Papa only looked at the total written at the bottom,

34
00:02:12,954 --> 00:02:16,510
and paid without asking any questions.

35
00:02:16,510 --> 00:02:19,959
Making charge means the labour for making the jewellery,

36
00:02:19,959 --> 00:02:24,393
the money for the craftsman's work. Gold is gold,

37
00:02:24,393 --> 00:02:27,841
but the engraving on the bangles, the lattice work on the necklace,

38
00:02:27,841 --> 00:02:32,275
all of this is handwork. The finer the design,

39
00:02:32,275 --> 00:02:37,202
the higher the making charge. And this money didn't go into the gold,

40
00:02:37,202 --> 00:02:38,680
it went into the design.

41
00:02:38,680 --> 00:02:42,664
Now here comes the thing nobody tells you.

42
00:02:42,664 --> 00:02:45,055
When you go to sell your jewellery,

43
00:02:45,055 --> 00:02:47,844
the jeweller only looks at the weight of the gold.

44
00:02:47,844 --> 00:02:50,633
The money you paid as making charges does not come back.

45
00:02:50,633 --> 00:02:55,016
On top of that, there may be some deduction on old jewellery,

46
00:02:55,016 --> 00:02:56,610
in the name of purity.

47
00:02:56,610 --> 00:02:59,770
Understand it like this: the day you bought the jewellery,

48
00:02:59,770 --> 00:03:04,284
that same day some of your money was gone forever.

49
00:03:04,284 --> 00:03:08,798
Only when the gold price goes up will that loss first get covered.

50
00:03:08,798 --> 00:03:11,957
Only after that will the real earning begin.

51
00:03:11,957 --> 00:03:16,020
So the race for jewellery starts from behind.

52
00:03:16,020 --> 00:03:18,394
It's the same story with GST.

53
00:03:18,394 --> 00:03:22,747
When buying, you paid GST on both the gold and the making charges.

54
00:03:22,747 --> 00:03:26,308
When selling, the jeweller does not give that GST back to you.

55
00:03:26,308 --> 00:03:30,265
That too is plain expense. On the bill it looks small,

56
00:03:30,265 --> 00:03:33,430
but years later, in the calculation, it looks big.

57
00:03:33,430 --> 00:03:37,403
So is buying jewellery wrong? Not at all.

58
00:03:37,403 --> 00:03:42,865
At your daughter's wedding, the shine of Mummy's bangle,

59
00:03:42,865 --> 00:03:48,328
its value can't be worked out on a calculator. It is happiness, a memory,

60
00:03:48,328 --> 00:03:53,294
a tradition. Just don't call it an investment. It is a purchase,

61
00:03:53,294 --> 00:03:55,280
like a new saree.

62
00:03:55,280 --> 00:03:56,453
Now the second question.

63
00:03:56,453 --> 00:04:01,144
After the wedding, Papa didn't feel it was right to keep the jewellery at home.

64
00:04:01,144 --> 00:04:04,662
There was fear of theft, and guests kept coming and going.

65
00:04:04,662 --> 00:04:08,572
So Papa went to the bank and asked the Bank Uncle for a locker.

66
00:04:08,572 --> 00:04:12,090
Bank Uncle gave a form and told him the yearly rent.

67
00:04:12,090 --> 00:04:19,395
At an SBI branch in a big city, the rent for a small locker is about 2,000 rupees a year.

68
00:04:19,395 --> 00:04:23,961
And even this 2,000 is not the full amount, GST is extra on top.

69
00:04:23,961 --> 00:04:27,614
Papa said, just this much? Okay, fine.

70
00:04:27,614 --> 00:04:32,180
And that rent started getting deducted from the account quietly every year.

71
00:04:32,180 --> 00:04:35,014
GST of 18 percent is charged on the locker,

72
00:04:35,014 --> 00:04:37,443
because it is a bank service.

73
00:04:37,443 --> 00:04:41,087
So the 2,000 rent actually turned out to be more than that.

74
00:04:41,087 --> 00:04:47,161
Papa never thought that this expense should also be counted against the gold.

75
00:04:47,161 --> 00:04:49,590
Truth be told, nobody thinks about it.

76
00:04:49,590 --> 00:04:53,280
This expense looks small, so it stays hidden.

77
00:04:53,280 --> 00:04:55,740
But it comes every year,

78
00:04:55,740 --> 00:04:58,610
whether the gold price goes up or down.

79
00:04:58,610 --> 00:05:01,890
As many years as the jewellery is in the locker, that many years of rent.

80
00:05:01,890 --> 00:05:06,810
And along with the locker key comes the time spent going to the bank,

81
00:05:06,810 --> 00:05:08,040
line and form.

82
00:05:08,040 --> 00:05:12,856
Now think, after many years Mummy sells the bangle.

83
00:05:12,856 --> 00:05:18,742
She sees the gold rate, gone up. But take off the making charge,

84
00:05:18,742 --> 00:05:23,558
GST, locker rent, and the cut when selling,

85
00:05:23,558 --> 00:05:25,164
all of this.

86
00:05:25,164 --> 00:05:31,050
Only then do you find out how much the jewellery actually earned.

87
00:05:31,050 --> 00:05:33,288
Bhai took out his phone and said,

88
00:05:33,288 --> 00:05:36,645
Gold goes up every year, so what's the problem?

89
00:05:36,645 --> 00:05:39,629
Behen immediately said, it doesn't go up every year,

90
00:05:39,629 --> 00:05:42,239
sometimes it falls too. And even if the rate goes up,

91
00:05:42,239 --> 00:05:44,477
earning is a different thing.

92
00:05:44,477 --> 00:05:48,580
Earning is what comes into your hand after all the expenses.

93
00:05:48,580 --> 00:05:51,952
Now the third question, where the story has a twist.

94
00:05:51,952 --> 00:05:56,590
Can there be gold that has no making charge,

95
00:05:56,590 --> 00:06:00,805
no locker, and on top of that gives you interest too? Yes,

96
00:06:00,805 --> 00:06:02,913
this is called paper gold.

97
00:06:02,913 --> 00:06:07,550
That means gold that is on paper or on a screen, not in the cupboard.

98
00:06:07,550 --> 00:06:10,895
The first form is the Sovereign Gold Bond, short name SGB.

99
00:06:10,895 --> 00:06:14,240
It is issued by the RBI on behalf of the government.

100
00:06:14,240 --> 00:06:16,470
RBI means the country's central bank,

101
00:06:16,470 --> 00:06:20,187
which is the bank of banks too. You don't buy gold,

102
00:06:20,187 --> 00:06:23,160
you buy bonds equal to grams of gold.

103
00:06:23,160 --> 00:06:27,633
The price of this bond moves with the gold rate.

104
00:06:27,633 --> 00:06:31,698
When gold gets costlier, the bond gets costlier. When gold gets cheaper,

105
00:06:31,698 --> 00:06:33,325
the bond gets cheaper too.

106
00:06:33,325 --> 00:06:37,391
So the risk on the gold is the same as with jewellery.

107
00:06:37,391 --> 00:06:41,050
Just no worry about making charge, locker and purity.

108
00:06:41,050 --> 00:06:44,586
Now the real twist. On top of the gold rate,

109
00:06:44,586 --> 00:06:48,564
SGB gives a fixed 2.5 percent interest every year.

110
00:06:48,564 --> 00:06:52,100
This interest is paid on your initial amount,

111
00:06:52,100 --> 00:06:55,636
that is, on what you bought the bond for.

112
00:06:55,636 --> 00:06:57,846
Jewellery doesn't give you any interest.

113
00:06:57,846 --> 00:07:00,940
It just sits in the locker.

114
00:07:00,940 --> 00:07:05,773
Understand it like this. Mummy's bangles are sleeping in the locker,

115
00:07:05,773 --> 00:07:07,969
and are asking for rent.

116
00:07:07,969 --> 00:07:11,045
The bond gold also sits quietly,

117
00:07:11,045 --> 00:07:14,999
but it pays 2.5 percent interest every year.

118
00:07:14,999 --> 00:07:19,392
The gold is the same in both places. But jewellery makes you spend,

119
00:07:19,392 --> 00:07:20,710
the bond earns.

120
00:07:20,710 --> 00:07:24,781
But there is a condition too, and listen to it carefully.

121
00:07:24,781 --> 00:07:27,947
This bond is meant for the long term.

122
00:07:27,947 --> 00:07:32,018
Breaking a bond early through the RBI, that is, premature redemption,

123
00:07:32,018 --> 00:07:36,089
is possible only after 5 years are complete.

124
00:07:36,089 --> 00:07:40,160
And that too only on the date when the interest is paid.

125
00:07:40,160 --> 00:07:40,974
This means,

126
00:07:40,974 --> 00:07:45,449
the money you need next year for a wedding or a house,

127
00:07:45,449 --> 00:07:47,891
is not meant for SGB.

128
00:07:47,891 --> 00:07:53,587
This bond is for money you can forget about for years.

129
00:07:53,587 --> 00:07:56,842
There is also the option of selling on the stock exchange,

130
00:07:56,842 --> 00:07:59,690
but there's no guarantee you'll find the right buyer there.

131
00:07:59,690 --> 00:08:03,358
And tax? This interest gets added to your income,

132
00:08:03,358 --> 00:08:07,841
and is taxed according to your slab.

133
00:08:07,841 --> 00:08:12,324
But at maturity, that is, when the bond's full term ends,

134
00:08:12,324 --> 00:08:16,807
the original buyer does not have to pay tax on capital gains.

135
00:08:16,807 --> 00:08:19,660
Capital gains means the profit made on selling.

136
00:08:19,660 --> 00:08:24,148
Brother said, I'll buy it tomorrow itself. Sister stopped him.

137
00:08:24,148 --> 00:08:27,005
New SGB issues don't come all the time,

138
00:08:27,005 --> 00:08:29,861
first check the RBI website.

139
00:08:29,861 --> 00:08:32,309
And if you buy an old bond from the exchange,

140
00:08:32,309 --> 00:08:35,982
the tax exemption rules can be different.

141
00:08:35,982 --> 00:08:38,430
Don't jump in on a tip without understanding.

142
00:08:38,430 --> 00:08:43,086
The other form is gold ETF. ETF means exchange traded fund,

143
00:08:43,086 --> 00:08:48,208
which is bought and sold on the stock exchange like a share.

144
00:08:48,208 --> 00:08:52,398
Behind every unit, real gold is held.

145
00:08:52,398 --> 00:08:57,520
For this you need a demat account, that is, a digital account to hold shares.

146
00:08:57,520 --> 00:09:01,451
In gold ETF too, there's no making charge, no locker,

147
00:09:01,451 --> 00:09:04,508
no worry about purity. And if you want to sell,

148
00:09:04,508 --> 00:09:08,002
you can sell when the market is open.

149
00:09:08,002 --> 00:09:09,749
But you get no interest,

150
00:09:09,749 --> 00:09:13,243
and a small yearly fund cost is deducted.

151
00:09:13,243 --> 00:09:17,610
This is called the expense ratio, that is, the fees for running the fund.

152
00:09:17,610 --> 00:09:22,968
Now look at everything together. Jewellery: the joy of wearing it,

153
00:09:22,968 --> 00:09:26,864
but making charge, GST and locker costs.

154
00:09:26,864 --> 00:09:31,248
Gold ETF: easy to sell, small fees, no interest.

155
00:09:31,248 --> 00:09:35,145
SGB: you get interest, tax exemption at maturity,

156
00:09:35,145 --> 00:09:37,580
but your money is stuck for a long time.

157
00:09:37,580 --> 00:09:41,910
Now the mistake that almost every household makes.

158
00:09:41,910 --> 00:09:45,279
We say, gold has earned so much,

159
00:09:45,279 --> 00:09:50,571
look at where the price has reached. But we only count the price.

160
00:09:50,571 --> 00:09:52,496
Making charge, GST, locker,

161
00:09:52,496 --> 00:09:57,308
And nobody counts the deductions when selling. Half the value lost,

162
00:09:57,308 --> 00:09:58,270
all the joy gone.

163
00:09:58,270 --> 00:10:01,454
Second mistake: treating jewellery as an emergency fund.

164
00:10:01,454 --> 00:10:04,638
Selling Mummy's bangle in hard times

165
00:10:04,638 --> 00:10:07,368
weighs heavy on the heart too.

166
00:10:07,368 --> 00:10:11,461
And then you have to sell on the jeweller's terms.

167
00:10:11,461 --> 00:10:15,555
For an emergency you need money that you can get immediately,

168
00:10:15,555 --> 00:10:16,920
without any loss.

169
00:10:16,920 --> 00:10:20,656
So what should we do? First, treat jewellery as jewellery.

170
00:10:20,656 --> 00:10:23,977
Buy it to wear, buy it for happiness.

171
00:10:23,977 --> 00:10:27,713
Buy hallmarked jewellery, and keep the bill safe.

172
00:10:27,713 --> 00:10:31,034
You can bargain on the making charges too.

173
00:10:31,034 --> 00:10:34,770
Before selling, ask different jewellers for their rates.

174
00:10:34,770 --> 00:10:37,972
Second thing, if you want gold for savings,

175
00:10:37,972 --> 00:10:40,773
then read up on paper gold.

176
00:10:40,773 --> 00:10:42,774
SGB for the long term,

177
00:10:42,774 --> 00:10:46,376
and gold ETF if you might need money soon.

178
00:10:46,376 --> 00:10:49,578
Understand the rules, tax and costs of both yourself.

179
00:10:49,578 --> 00:10:53,580
If needed, talk to your CA or adviser.

180
00:10:53,580 --> 00:10:57,228
Third thing, don't put all your savings into gold.

181
00:10:57,228 --> 00:10:59,965
Gold is a companion in hard times,

182
00:10:59,965 --> 00:11:02,701
but its price can fall too,

183
00:11:02,701 --> 00:11:06,805
and it can stay flat for years. A little gold,

184
00:11:06,805 --> 00:11:10,910
the rest in different places. This is not investment advice.

185
00:11:10,910 --> 00:11:13,190
It's just common sense.

186
00:11:13,190 --> 00:11:18,543
At the end of the story, Mummy did not sell the bangle. She said,

187
00:11:18,543 --> 00:11:21,949
this will go for my daughter's wedding.

188
00:11:21,949 --> 00:11:26,328
But next time if gold is needed for savings,

189
00:11:26,328 --> 00:11:30,707
she will sit with her sister and understand paper gold.

190
00:11:30,707 --> 00:11:34,600
Bangle for love, bond for earning.

191
00:11:34,600 --> 00:11:35,918
Now a question for you.

192
00:11:35,918 --> 00:11:40,310
In what form is gold at your home: jewellery, coin,

193
00:11:40,310 --> 00:11:44,263
ETF or bond? Just write that word in the comments.

194
00:11:44,263 --> 00:11:46,019
And also tell me,

195
00:11:46,019 --> 00:11:51,290
has anyone at your home ever counted the locker rent?

196
00:11:51,290 --> 00:11:55,432
In the next video it's Papa's FD's turn.

197
00:11:55,432 --> 00:11:57,273
An FD feels safe,

198
00:11:57,273 --> 00:12:01,415
but after cutting inflation, how much is actually left?

199
00:12:01,415 --> 00:12:06,478
That story too will be like this, from inside the home. Until then,

200
00:12:06,478 --> 00:12:10,620
find your jewellery bill and keep it, it will come in handy.
